{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי גרים ותושבים אתם עמדי", :translit "ki gerim v'toshavim atem imadi", :gloss "for strangers and settlers you are with Me"} {:he "ובכל ארץ אחוזתכם", :translit "uv'chol eretz achuzatchem", :gloss "and in all the land of your possession"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: adjacent verses read together — 'with Me' (Lev 25:23) joined to 'your possession' (Lev 25:24) to infer the Shekhinah accompanies exile"}], :frame {:text "The principle of semikhut parshiyot reads adjacent verses as contextually linked. The closing words of Leviticus 25:23, 'with Me' (עמדי), are read against the opening of Leviticus 25:24, 'your possession' (אחוזתכם), to yield the inference that God's presence remains with Israel wherever they hold possession — even in exile.", :sources ["Leviticus 25:23" "Leviticus 25:24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: adjacent verses read together — 'with Me' (Lev 25:23) joined to 'your possession' (Lev 25:24) to infer the Shekhinah accompanies exile", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:33.926457626Z", :model "glm-5.2"}